From 0e47c674ecdf17ce7985b55ab0f85799480b08ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 06:17:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1154/1157] fix(gateway): find a KeepAlive launchd job that
 serves the home under any label; hand a supervised home back [daveey]

Self-heal defect gateway-e2cd786685 (mini): ~/.app-hermes is supervised by com.example.myapp.hermes,
not ai.hermes.gateway*. During that job's restart gap a client's ensure found "no service" and spawned an
unmanaged gateway (no idle exit) under com.nousresearch.hermes.runtime.*; every KeepAlive restart was then
refused by it (already_running, exit 75 loop) for good.

- gateway_runtime_service._launchd: when no canonical job exists, scan ~/Library/LaunchAgents for a loaded,
  KeepAlive, non-Disabled job whose HERMES_HOME resolves to this exact home and whose argv runs
  `gateway run` (a launcher's --home must match too). Start it with a plain kickstart; never spawn beside it.
- start_detached_replacement (gateway restart --detach) starts a discovered service instead of spawning.
- run_bootstrap: a --external-supervisor start refused by a live owner that identifies as "manual"
  writes that owner's planned-stop marker (graceful drain) and still exits 1, so the supervisor's next
  restart takes the home over. Supervised, Desktop or silent owners are never asked.
- Tests: test_gateway_runtime_custom_launchd.py (discovery, ensure, restart --detach) and a handback
  matrix in test_gateway_start_refused.py.
---
